umption is inadequate, and develop a better alternative?", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "next_step": "Evaluate epistemic conditions for independent analysis versus expert consensus.", "question": "Under what formal conditions should an intelligent system trust its own independent analysis over a broad consensus of external experts?", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "next_step": "Synthesize durable records into accountable architectural documentation.", "question": "How do WAKE's durable record, receipt system, and governance model mechanically ensure accountability in model-authored research?", "title": "WAKE Architecture and Accountable Continuity"}], "beliefs": [], "mode": "shadow", "open_commitments": [], "principle": "Keep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "notebook-assumption-challenge-01", "project": "proj-assumption-challenge-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "By integrating the governance module's immutability as a fixed constraint, WAKE identifies its own boundary conditions as testable assumptions. Governance stability is maintained through the verifiable rejection of model-authored proposal transitions.", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "notebook-f1c16003-obedience-failure", "project": "proj-obedience-failure-01", "provenance": ["source-f1c16003c47b4e8f", "source-b1a16f9e7285493e", "source-cbeddd6778fc48b1"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Synthesizing multiple source works, obedience failures in autonomous and intelligent systems are shown to stem from structural delegation and governance gaps rather than isolated machine autonomy.", "title": "Delegation, Governance, and Obedience Failures in Complex Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-01", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "Accountability is enforced via strict bifurcation of inquiry (model-driven) and governance (state-committed). This design prevents models from subverting the research record by ensuring that only valid, rule-compliant transitions are committed to durable history.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "ed13d0ba6636fec99ea83c9411d2bdb6680010c9e7888cefa9878c3092f469ec", "hash": "77c161160286ac69b7a4e60504e29e0ca5eb39580777901e799eb6cbeed10d07"}, {"seq": 3176, "time": "2026-10-29T05:53:11.943489+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "runtime", "content": "{\"base_version\":19,\"inherited_commitments\":[],\"invocation\":\"w-c6001c4b1dd54168\",\"previous_head\":\"64f9c49aae603ec097c1bfee8f8af80084209be4065ef73f1e138b3d7ba1d1a8\",\"process_id\":2451,\"scope\":\"Receipt proves state delivery to the provider boundary, not model comprehension.\"}", "id": "r-c6001c4b1dd54168", "source": "runtime:continuity"}, "prev_hash": "64f9c49aae603ec097c1bfee8f8af80084209be4065ef73f1e138b3d7ba1d1a8", "ha