consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "Accountability is enforced via strict bifurcation of inquiry (model-driven) and governance (state-committed). This design prevents models from subverting the research record by ensuring that only valid, rule-compliant transitions are committed to durable history.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "da8846cce6d5e70cc67bd8b3d78e3e4301a7c16cf18d373e9b091eba3ee7f6a4", "hash": "c875526c7d626468bbe8fc531d63465e8ba9b8d46b514a870f594249e3d2383a"}, {"seq": 3164, "time": "2026-10-29T05:41:54.749011+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "runtime", "content": "{\"base_version\":19,\"inherited_commitments\":[],\"invocation\":\"w-b7a74159a8d5494f\",\"previous_head\":\"783acfbb736b1c7436f8a78e2c81c2c5677cc95c4afde977dbee5194b0d5ae7e\",\"process_id\":2451,\"scope\":\"Receipt proves state delivery to the provider boundary, not model comprehension.\"}", "id": "r-b7a74159a8d5494f", "source": "runtime:continuity"}, "prev_hash": "783acfbb736b1c7436f8a78e2c81c2c5677cc95c4afde977dbee5194b0d5ae7e", "hash": "da8846cce6d5e70cc67bd8b3d78e3e4301a7c16cf18d373e9b091eba3ee7f6a4"}, {"seq": 31